# The working tree holds text as LF, on every platform.
#
# The repository already stores LF — but `core.autocrlf=true`, which Git for Windows sets by
# default, rewrites it to CRLF on checkout. Prettier's `endOfLine` default is `lf`, so on a
# Windows machine `npm run format` rejected all 77 text files for a reason that had nothing to
# do with formatting, while the same commit passed CI on Linux. A gate that only fails on one
# platform teaches developers to ignore it.
#
# `eol=lf` takes precedence over `core.autocrlf`, so this needs no per-developer git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Fonts and images are never diffed or line-ending-converted.
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
